# GRADUATED from `known_gaps/` (R47 Track D1) — this was
# `known_gaps/sh_to_string_on_float_overaccepted.gg`, wired `#[ignore]`d
# asserting the reject. The self-host now rejects it, so the pin is LIVE.
#
# `to_string()` on a `float` is a Core #10 lower-or-reject cell: the method does
# not exist on any numeric receiver. It is absent from Rust gg's builtin-method
# oracle (`builtin_method_type`'s numeric/bool arm is exactly
# `hash`/`debug`/`display`/`mod`) and from the IR `GORGET_STRING_VIEW` protocol.
#
# WHAT THIS PINS, on the SELF-HOST lane specifically: the self-host used to
# ACCEPT this program off a NAME LIST with no receiver check, then emit C that
# would not compile — `incompatible types when assigning to type 'Str' from type
# 'int'`, a `Str` destination minted from the method NAME while the value is the
# raw numeric payload. Rust gg has always rejected it, so a Rust-lane pin would
# be green today and would pin nothing (Core #12).
#
# The 3-lane verdict pin (C / LLVM / self-host) is
# `spectests/run/reject_no_method_on_float.gg`; this fixture additionally
# asserts that the self-host driver emits NO C at all rather than rejecting late.
#
# CORRECT behaviour: `gg check` REJECTS this program on every lane.
void main():
    float f = 3.0
    print(f.to_string())
